      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $5$ must have at least $5$ columns and at least $5$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $B$ since it has only $2$ rows. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $5$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $A$ has only $4$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(A)=4.$ As we can see, the matrix $C$ has exactly $5$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\"",
